body: "## Static finding at PR #148\n\nReviewed current head `0fa008998f4b6991bcaec8532012f28100ad75e9` of [PR #148](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/148). This is an exact-source capacity finding plus a dependency-free byte calculation, **not an actual SDK/controller reproduction**.\n\nThe [documented design](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/0fa008998f4b6991bcaec8532012f28100ad75e9/docs/proposer-transfer.md) requires 3,062 independent trackers per task and per look for one generation plus audit, and preserves native digest-only replay. Raising the task representation bound to 10,000 does not make that population archivable.\n\n## Exact evidence\n\n- [The fixed power calculation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/0fa008998f4b6991bcaec8532012f28100ad75e9/proposer-transfer.ts#L67-L76) gives 3,062 trackers with two looks.\n- Each task has one target. Both targets therefore require at least 6,124 tasks in meta and 6,124 in audit: **12,248 references**, even with each tracker contributing both targets.\n- [archiveTransferCorpus](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/0fa008998f4b6991bcaec8532012f28100ad75e9/proposer-transfer.ts#L130-L138) puts every `{role,digest}` reference, plus the complete manifest, into one corpus record and preflights that record against [MAX_TRACKER_RECORD_BYTES = 1,048,576](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/0fa008998f4b6991bcaec8532012f28100ad75e9/tracker-record.ts#L4-L7).\n- The minimum meta/audit references alone encode to **1,132,941 UTF-8 bytes**, already **84,365 bytes over** the limit, before the manifest, development references or enclosing record fields.\n\nA standalone Node calculation of that strict lower bound:\n\n```js\nconst minimumTrackers = 3062;\nconst references = [\"meta\", \"audit\"].flatMap(role =>\n  Array.from({ length: 2 * minimumTrackers }, () => ({\n    role, digest: \"a\".repeat(64)\n  }))\n);\nconsole.log(references.length);                       // 12248\nconsole.log(Buffer.byteLength(JSON.stringify(references))); // 1132941\n```\n\nThe repeated dummy digest measures fixed-width encoding only; this is not a valid corpus or synthetic transfer-efficacy result. The exact source power function was separately evaluated without dependencies and returned 3,062. No native writes, learner fits or full release suite were run for this finding.\n\n## Expected, actual and impact\n\nExpected: a valid, supported minimum powered corpus can be archived and reconstructed from native records without relaxing record limits.\n\nActual: the single corpus manifest necessarily exceeds its one-MiB preflight bound at that minimum. Even supplying sufficient independently justified public sources cannot unblock this path. The current powered synthetic control evaluates an in-memory corpus without archiving it, so it does not cover this boundary.\n\nThe [corpus-scale follow-up](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/0fa008998f4b6991bcaec8532012f28100ad75e9/.agents/pm/tasks/pm-rl-rsipower-corpus-scale.toon) owns source acquisition and independence. This issue isolates the additional storage-format blocker, with PR #148 retaining implementation ownership. It does not challenge the intentionally underpowered diagnostic or claim overspend, promotion or transfer efficacy.\n\n## Acceptance / regression criteria\n\n1. Add a real-SDK regression using a valid minimum powered meta/audit population plus a valid development compartment. Archive, load and digest-only replay must succeed within all existing native record limits.\n2. Use bounded digest-addressed manifest/reference chunks or an equivalent bounded representation, retaining immutable history, exact source/split identities, complete integrity checks and compatibility with existing receipts.\n3. Cover chunk boundaries and missing, duplicated, reordered, tampered or oversized references without partial success being mistaken for a complete archive.\n4. Preserve the one-MiB record cap, existing statistical/resource gates and fail-closed behavior. Do not weaken power thresholds to make the fixture fit.\n\nDuplicate check: all 148 open/closed GitHub issues and PRs, current PR discussion and review threads, and 129 canonical planning/approval/result records. No existing owner of this specific manifest-capacity finding was found; broader source-scale work and the earlier byte-preflight hardening remain separate."
